# Code owners approve every pull request. This is the mechanism that keeps merging
# a human decision: an agent working under a separate identity is not listed here,
# so it cannot approve, and GitHub never lets anyone approve their own pull request.
#
# Both humans are listed on purpose. With a single code owner, that owner's own pull
# requests would be unmergeable: the "require code owner review" rule on main has an
# empty bypass list, and nobody can approve their own pull request. Two owners mean a
# pull request opened by one is always approvable by the other.
